.. sidebar:: ScenerySketching:: CodeAI
   :class: sidebar-ScenerySketching

   .. Zo'n 160 woorden -- komt terug in elke blog

   Software engineers use interfaces such as APIs.
   But also meta-interfaces -- like your editor;
   it’s the interface between the team and
   the code it produces. That meta-interface
   determines how *efficiently* you work.

   Every AI provider promises new “silver bullets”
   to make coding trivial. But, does it work --
   outside the trivial examples they show? Does it
   work for us?
   |BR|
   Or should we stick to our familiar, trusted gear
   for the embedded, sovereign software we work on?
   |BR|
   Like our electrical coworkers – even though AI
   can generate diagrams, I have never seen a PCB
   design made by AI …

   We can't deny CodeAI is coming. The question is,
   can we use it to become more efficient? Or will
   mastering them consume more time than they can
   ever save you?

   In this :ref:`series <ScenerySketching_CodeAI>`,
   I sketch the scenery as a Holistic Architectural
   Leader, skipping constantly changing details.

   My goal is simple: boost that ‘golden’
   controlled approach to rocket speed.


